messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B or C.\n####\n# Context:\nThe cat chases the dog. The cat chases the mouse. The cat chases the tiger. The cat eats the dog. The dog is big. The dog sees the cat. The mouse does not eat the cat. The mouse eats the tiger. The mouse does not see the tiger. The tiger eats the dog. The tiger is nice. If something is young and it eats the tiger then it eats the dog. If something sees the mouse and it eats the mouse then the mouse sees the tiger. If something sees the mouse then it is big. If something chases the dog then the dog chases the cat. If something chases the dog then it chases the cat. If something chases the tiger and the tiger eats the cat then the cat sees the mouse. If something sees the dog and it chases the tiger then the tiger chases the dog. If the tiger is green and the tiger is big then the tiger sees the dog. If something chases the cat then it sees the dog.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or unknown? The tiger does not see the dog.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Unknown', '<think>\nOkay, so I have this logical reasoning problem to solve.Let me try to break it down step by step.The question is whether the statement "The tiger does not see the dog" is true, false, or unknown based on the given context.The options are A) True, B) False, C) Unknown.\n\nFirst, I\'ll read through the context carefully to understand all the given information.There are several statements here, some of which are facts, and others that seem to be implications or rules.I need to parse each one and see how they relate to the question.\n\nLet me list out all the context statements:\n\n1.The cat chases the dog.\n2.The cat chases the mouse.\n3.The cat chases the tiger.\n4.The cat eats the dog.\n5.The dog is big.\n6.The dog sees the cat.\n7.The mouse does not eat the cat.\n8.The mouse eats the tiger.\n9.The mouse does not see the tiger.\n10.The tiger eats the dog.\n11.The tiger is nice.\n12.If something is young and it eats the tiger then it eats the dog.\n13.If something sees the mouse and it eats the mouse then the mouse sees the tiger.\n14.If something sees the mouse then it is big.\n15.If something chases the dog then the dog chases the cat.\n16.If something chases the dog then it chases the cat.\n17.If something chases the tiger and the tiger eats the cat then the cat sees the mouse.\n18.If something sees the dog and it chases the tiger then the tiger chases the dog.\n19.If the tiger is green and the tiger is big then the tiger sees the dog.\n20.If something chases the cat then it sees the dog.\n\nNow, the question is about whether the tiger does not see the dog.So I need to determine if the tiger sees the dog or not, based on the context.\n\nLet me go through each relevant statement and see what I can deduce.\n\nStarting with the facts:\n\n- The dog is big (statement 5).\n- The dog sees the cat (statement 6).\n- The tiger eats the dog (statement 10).\n- The tiger is nice (statement 11).\n- The mouse does not see the tiger (statement 9).\n- The mouse eats the tiger (statement 8).\n- The cat eats the dog (statement 4).\n- The cat chases the dog (statement 1), the cat chases the mouse (statement 2), and the cat chases the tiger (statement 3).\n\nNow, looking at the implications:\n\n12.If something is young and it eats the tiger then it eats the dog.\n13.If something sees the mouse and it eats the mouse then the mouse sees the tiger.\n14.If something sees the mouse then it is big.\n15.If something chases the dog then the dog chases the cat.\n16.If something chases the dog then it chases the cat.\n17.If something chases the tiger and the tiger eats the cat then the cat sees the mouse.\n18.If something sees the dog and it chases the tiger then the tiger chases the dog.\n19.If the tiger is green and the tiger is big then the tiger sees the dog.\n20.If something chases the cat then it sees the dog.\n\nI need to see if any of these implications can help determine whether the tiger sees the dog.\n\nFirst, let\'s consider the facts.The tiger eats the dog (10), and the dog is big (5).The cat chases the dog (1), and the cat eats the dog (4).So the cat is chasing the dog and eating it.The cat does not see the dog, so the cat is not aware of the dog.</think>\n\nThe statement "The tiger does not see the dog" is false because, based on the context, the tiger chases the dog, which implies the tiger sees the dog.. Therefore, my final option is: ']]  2%|1         | 11/600 [00:18<21:34,  2.20s/it]
