 is rough (15)\n- Harry is smart (16)\n\nSo, from the given facts, Harry is quiet.But wait, the question is whether the statement "Harry is not quiet" is true, false, or unknown.So, if Harry is quiet, then the statement "Harry is not quiet" would be false.\n\nBut I should also check if there\'s any information that might affect this conclusion.Let\'s look at the implications.\n\nFrom statement 17: If someone is rough, then they are cold.So, being rough implies being cold.Harry is not quiet.</think>\n\nThe statement "Harry is not quiet" is false because the context explicitly states that Harry is quiet.. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
