      "text": " A) True.\n\n**Step-by-Step Explanation:**\n\n1. **Gary is smart (point 7).**\n2. **All smart things are furry (point 8).** Therefore, Gary is furry.\n3. **If Gary is furry (point 12), then he is blue.** So, Gary is blue.\n4. **Big, blue things are round (point 9).** Since Gary is blue, he must be big and round.\n5. **Round things are cold (point 13).** Therefore, Gary is cold.\n6. **If Gary is cold (point 10), then he is smart.** Which we already know from point 7.\n7. **Cold, white things are furry (point 14).** Since Gary is cold and furry, he must be white.\n8. **Anne is white (point 4).** But there's no direct link between Gary and Anne's size.\n9. **Big, blue things are round (point 9).** Since Gary is blue and big, he's round.\n10. **Round things are cold (point 13).** So Gary is cold.\n11. **If Gary is cold (point 10), then he is smart.** Which we've established.\n12. **All blue, furry things are big (point 11).** Gary is blue and furry, so he's big.\n\nTherefore, Gary is big, making the statement true.\n</think>\n\nThe statement \"Gary is big\" is **True**.\n\n**Answer: A) True**",
