      "text": " B) False.\n\n**Step-by-Step Explanation:**\n\n1. **Identify all given information:**\n   - Bob is big, blue, rough, and smart.\n   - Blue, round people are rough.\n   - If someone is round, then they are blue.\n   - Blue, round people are big.\n   - If someone is blue, then they are young.\n   - Charlie is smart.\n   - Smart people are quiet.\n   - If someone is smart and quiet, then they are young.\n   - All rough, young people are round.\n   - Smart people are rough.\n\n2. **Analyze Bob's attributes:**\n   - Bob is smart (point 5) and rough (point 4), which aligns with point 15 (smart people are rough).\n   - Since Bob is blue (point 3) and round (from points 8 and 11), he is big (point 2 and 16).\n\n3. **Determine Charlie's attributes:**\n   - Charlie is smart (point 6), so he must be quiet (point 10).\n   - Being smart and quiet makes Charlie young (point 9).\n   - From point 13, if someone is blue, they are young. Since Charlie is young, he could be blue, but it's not necessarily concluded yet.\n\n4. **Check if Charlie must be blue:**\n   - Point 11 states that if someone is round, they are blue. Since all rough, young people are round (point 14), and Charlie is young and rough (as smart people are rough, point 15), Charlie must be round.\n   - Therefore, Charlie is round, which implies he is blue (point 11).\n   - Hence, Charlie is blue, making the statement \"Charlie is not blue\" false.\n\n**Answer:** B) False",
