ll nice things are blue. So, if Anne is nice, she must be blue and rough.\n\n6. **Contradiction:**\n   - Anne is green and quiet.\n   - If Anne is nice, she must be blue and rough.\n   - But blue and rough things are not necessarily green or quiet. There is no direct contradiction here.\n\n7. **Conclusion:**\n   - The context does not provide direct information about whether Anne is nice or not.\n   - Therefore, the statement \"Anne is nice\" is **unknown** based on the given information.\n\n**Final Answer:**\n\\boxed{C}",
