      "text": " A) True.\n</think>\n\nLet's analyze the given context and determine whether the statement \"The squirrel does not see the bear\" is true, false, or unknown.\n\n### Context Analysis:\n\n1. **Bear sees the squirrel.**\n2. **Bear visits the rabbit.**\n3. **Lion is not round.**\n4. **Lion does not like the rabbit.**\n5. **Lion visits the bear.**\n6. **Rabbit is not big.**\n7. **Rabbit is kind.**\n8. **Rabbit likes the squirrel.**\n9. **Rabbit sees the bear.**\n10. **Rabbit does not visit the bear.**\n11. **Squirrel visits the lion.**\n12. **If something is big and it visits the lion then the lion visits the rabbit.**\n13. **If something sees the lion then it does not like the lion.**\n14. **If something likes the squirrel then the squirrel visits the rabbit.**\n15. **If something sees the squirrel and it visits the squirrel then the squirrel does not see the lion.**\n16. **If something visits the lion then the lion is not round.**\n17. **If something sees the lion and it does not see the bear then it sees the squirrel.**\n18. **If something visits the rabbit then it sees the lion.**\n19. **If something sees the lion then it is big.**\n\n### Key Points:\n\n- **Bear sees the squirrel (1).**\n- **Rabbit sees the bear (9).**\n- **Rabbit does not visit the bear (10).**\n- **Squirrel visits the lion (11).**\n- **If something sees the squirrel and it visits the squirrel, then the squirrel does not see the lion (15).**\n\n### Reasoning:\n\n- From point **1**, the bear sees the squirrel.\n- From point **9**, the rabbit sees the bear.\n- From point **10**, the rabbit does not visit the bear.\n- From point **11**, the squirrel visits the lion.\n- From point **15**, if something sees the squirrel and visits the squirrel, then the squirrel does not see the lion.\n\n### Conclusion:\n\n- The squirrel visits the lion (11).\n- The squirrel does not see the lion based on point **15**.\n- Since the squirrel does not see the lion, it implies that the squirrel does not see the bear.\n\n### Final Answer:\n\n**The statement \"The squirrel does not see the bear\" is **True**.**\n\n\\boxed{A) True}",
