s green, she is furry.\n\n12. **From statement 1: Anne is furry.**\n    - Since all furry things are green, Anne is green.\n\n13. **From statement 15: Green things are red.**\n    - Since Anne is green, she is red.\n\n14. **From statement 2: Anne is smart.**\n    - Since Anne is red, from statement 13, she is smart.\n\n15. **From statement 8: All smart, round things are not nice.**\n    - Since Anne is smart and round (from statement 14), she is not nice.\n\n### Conclusion:\n\n- **Fiona is not red** because:\n  - Fiona is not smart (from step 6).\n  - If Fiona were red, she would be smart (from statement 13), which contradicts step 6.\n  - Therefore, Fiona cannot be red.\n\n**Final Answer:**  \n\\boxed{B) False}",
