statement 11 says if someone is green and not big, they are kind.Erin is green and not big, so she is kind.So, Erin is kind.\n\nWait, but the question is about Gary, not Erin.So, let\'s see if Gary\'s coldness connects to any of these traits.\n\nLooking at statement 12: If someone is kind and not big, then they are round.We know Erin is kind and not big, so she is round (statement 6).But how does this help with Gary?\n\nGary is unkind.</think>.\n\nThe statement "Gary is kind" cannot be determined from the given context, as there is no direct information linking Gary to being kind. Therefore, the answer is:. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
