      "text": " Gary is not white. Based on the context, Gary is cold and quiet. Since rough, white things are cold, and Gary is cold, Gary must be rough. Being rough implies Gary is young. All young things are round, so Gary is round. Additionally, if something is round and rough, it is nice. Therefore, Gary is nice. Nice things are white, so Gary is white. Since Gary is white, the statement \"Gary is not white\" is false.\n</think>\n\n**Answer: B) False**\n\n**Explanation:**\n\n1. **Gary's Attributes:**\n   - Gary is cold.\n   - Gary is quiet.\n\n2. **Rough and White Things:**\n   - Rough, white things are cold.\n   - Since Gary is cold and fits the description of a rough, white thing, Gary must be rough.\n\n3. **Implications of Being Rough:**\n   - If something is rough, it is young.\n   - Therefore, Gary is young.\n\n4. **Round and Rough Things:**\n   - All young things are round.\n   - So, Gary is round.\n\n5. **Round and Rough Imply Nice:**\n   - If something is round and rough, it is nice.\n   - Hence, Gary is nice.\n\n6. **Nice Things:**\n   - Nice things are white.\n   - Therefore, Gary is white.\n\n7. **Conclusion:**\n   - The statement \"Gary is not white\" is false because Gary is white.",
