messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B or C.\n####\n# Context:\nThe cat is nice. The cat needs the lion. The cat visits the lion. The cow is nice. The cow needs the cat. The lion is nice. The lion is red. The lion is young. The lion needs the cow. The lion needs the squirrel. The squirrel is young. If the cow needs the lion then the lion visits the squirrel. If something needs the squirrel then it visits the cat. If something needs the cow and it chases the squirrel then the cow is rough. If something chases the squirrel and it is young then the squirrel needs the cat. If something visits the cow then it is rough. If the squirrel visits the cat and the cat is red then the squirrel chases the cow. All nice things are big. If something is big then it visits the squirrel. If something visits the cat and the cat visits the squirrel then the squirrel is nice.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or unknown? The squirrel is not big.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Unknown', '<think>\nOkay, so I have this logical reasoning problem to solve.Let me try to break it down step by step.The problem gives me a context with several statements and then asks a question about whether a specific statement is true, false, or unknown.The question is: "The squirrel is not big."The options are A) True, B) False, C) Unknown.\n\nFirst, I need to understand all the given information.Let me list out the context statements:\n\n1.The cat is nice.\n2.The cat needs the lion.\n3.The cat visits the lion.\n4.The cow is nice.\n5.The cow needs the cat.\n6.The lion is nice.\n7.The lion is red.\n8.The lion is young.\n9.The lion needs the cow.\n10.The lion needs the squirrel.\n11.The squirrel is young.\n12.If the cow needs the lion, then the lion visits the squirrel.\n13.If something needs the squirrel, then it visits the cat.\n14.If something needs the cow and it chases the squirrel, then the cow is rough.\n15.If something chases the squirrel and it is young, then the squirrel needs the cat.\n16.If something visits the cow, then it is rough.\n17.If the squirrel visits the cat and the cat is red, then the squirrel chases the cow.\n18.All nice things are big.\n19.If something is big, then it visits the squirrel.\n20.If something visits the cat and the cat visits the squirrel, then the squirrel is nice.\n\nAlright, that\'s a lot.Now, I need to figure out whether the squirrel is big or not.The question is whether the statement "The squirrel is not big" is true, false, or unknown based on the context.\n\nLet me start by looking for any direct statements about the squirrel\'s size.From the context, I see that the squirrel is young (statement 11).But that doesn\'t directly tell me if it\'s big or not.Also, statement 19 says that if something is big, it visits the squirrel.So, if something is big, it goes to the squirrel.But does that mean the squirrel is big?Not necessarily.It just means that big things visit the squirrel.\n\nLooking further, statement 20 says that if something visits the cat and the cat visits the squirrel, then the squirrel is nice.So, visiting the squirrel makes the squirrel nice, but that doesn\'t say anything about size.\n\nNow, let\'s look at the implications.Statement 12: If the cow needs the lion, then the lion visits the squirrel.So, the lion visiting the squirrel is a consequence of the cow needing the lion.But I\'m not sure how that ties into the squirrel\'s size.\n\nStatement 13: If something needs the squirrel, then it visits the cat.So, needing the squirrel leads to visiting the cat.Again, not directly about size.\n\nStatement 14: If something needs the cow and it chases the squirrel, then the cow is rough.So, chasing the squirrel when needing the cow makes the cow rough.Not directly about size.\n\nStatement 15: If something chases the squirrel and it\'s young, then the squirrel needs the cat.So, chasing a young squirrel leads to the squirrel needing the cat.Still not about size.The squirrel is big based on the given information.</think>.\n\nThe context does not provide direct information about the squirrel\'s size, only that it is young and that other animals (cat, lion, cow) are big. Therefore, my final option is: ']] 55%|#####4    | 329/600 [23:43<1:02:52, 13.92s/it]
