7). So, the cat chases the squirrel, which makes the squirrel visit the cat. Then, from statement 14, if something visits the cat, it likes the cat. So, the squirrel visits the cat, so the squirrel likes the cat. Therefore, the statement is true. So, the answer is A) True.\n\nWait, that seems to make sense. Let me recap:\n\n- The cat chases the squirrel (from statement 17, since the cat likes the cat, so it chases the squirrel).\n- The squirrel is chased by the cat, so the squirrel visits the cat (from statement 20).\n- Since the squirrel visits the cat, the squirrel likes the cat (from statement 14).\nTherefore, the statement is true.\n\nSo, the answer is A) True.\n</think>\n\nThe squirrel likes the cat because the cat chases the squirrel, which causes the squirrel to visit the cat. Since visiting the cat implies liking it, the statement is true.\n\n**Answer: A) True**",
