is green, so from statement 16, if someone is green, they are big.Therefore, Fiona is big.\n- Since Fiona is big, from statement 19, all green, big people are round.Therefore, Fiona is round.\n\nWait, that seems straightforward.So Fiona is green, which makes her big, and all green big people are round, so Fiona is round.That would make the statement "Fiona is round" true, so the answer should be A) True.\n\nBut let me double-check to make sure I didn\'t miss anything.Sometimes these logic problems have hidden connections or implications that aren\'t immediately obvious.\n\nLooking at the other statements, let\'s see if there\'s any information that could affect Fiona\'s roundness.Fiona is not green, so she is not big, and big green people are not round, so Fiona is not round. Therefore, the answer should be B) False.</think>\n\nThe statement "Fiona is round" is true based on the given information.. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
