t point 3: Erin is not round.Erin is red (point 2), so Erin is red and not round.Point 12 says if Erin is young and round, then Erin is blue.But Erin is not round, so that condition doesn\'t apply to Erin.However, Erin is red, and point 15 says rough things are not red.So Erin is red, but since Erin is not round, maybe that\'s a clue.\n\nPoint 14: Round, quiet things are young.So if something is round and quiet, it\'s young.Since Harry is young, maybe Harry is round and quiet.But let\'s see.Harry is round.</think>\n\nThe statement "Harry is not round" is true because if Harry were round, he would have to be blue, which contradicts the given information that Harry is not blue.. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
